WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:08.080 align:start position:19%
Nine experienced hikers walked into the
Eural Mountains in 1959. None of them

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:14.960 align:start position:19%
ever came home. What searchers found
weeks later defied every explanation and

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:20.000 align:start position:19%
still does 67 years on. This is the
Diatlov Pass incident. The most chilling

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:25.519 align:start position:19%
unsolved mystery in mountaineering
history. Igor Yatlov, a 23-year-old

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:30.720 align:start position:19%
engineering student, assembled a team of
the country's finest young hikers. Eight

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:35.360 align:start position:19%
men and two women, all seasoned in
brutal winter survival, all hungry for

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:40.399 align:start position:19%
the highest climbing certification.
Their goal, Mount Otton, a remote peak

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:45.840 align:start position:19%
in the northern Eurals in the dead of
the Russian winter. On January 23rd, the

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:50.559 align:start position:19%
group left the town of Ifdell, riding
trucks and skis into the frozen unknown.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:57.120 align:start position:19%
One member would never reach the
mountain. Yuri Yudin fell ill and turned

00:00:53.840 --> 00:01:03.520 align:start position:19%
back. It saved his life. Udin watched
his nine friends ski into the white

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:09.520 align:start position:19%
silence. The last person to see them
alive. The nine pressed on, keeping a

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:16.080 align:start position:19%
cheerful diary. On February 1st, they
camped on Kolatak's slope. In the Many

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:21.280 align:start position:19%
language, Colatsak means dead mountain.
The hikers didn't know or didn't care.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:27.520 align:start position:19%
That night, temperatures plunged to
minus30. Inside the tent, they ate,

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:34.320 align:start position:19%
joked, and wrote journals. One diary
entry read, "We know now that snowmen

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:40.000 align:start position:19%
exist. They were in high spirits. Then
nothing, silence." On February 20th, a

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:45.680 align:start position:19%
search party of students and soldiers
set out into the frozen eurals. 6 days

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:50.960 align:start position:19%
later they found the tent half
collapsed, half buried on the slope of

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:56.240 align:start position:19%
the dead mountain. The tent was slashed
open from the inside.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:02:02.640 align:start position:19%
Long, desperate cuts as if they'd fled
in blind panic. Inside, boots, warm

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:07.439 align:start position:19%
clothes, food, money, cameras,
everything abandoned. People don't leave

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:12.480 align:start position:19%
survival gear behind. Outside,
footprints led downhill toward the

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:19.040 align:start position:19%
forest. Some in socks, some in a single
boot, one completely barefoot. In

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:25.120 align:start position:19%
minus30 cold, barefoot in the snow means
death within minutes. Yet they ran away

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:30.160 align:start position:19%
from the tent. Something had terrified
nine fearless mountaineers so completely

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:36.160 align:start position:19%
that shelter became more frightening
than the storm. A mile downhill stood a

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:42.000 align:start position:19%
giant cedar tree. Beneath it, searchers
found the first two bodies. Yuri

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:46.400 align:start position:19%
Creonenko and Yuri Dorosenko, sholess in
underwear, their hands burned from

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:52.480 align:start position:19%
clawing at frozen branches. They climbed
the cedar in desperation to see the tent

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:58.400 align:start position:19%
or to escape something on the ground.
Between the cedar and the tent lay three

00:02:54.959 --> 00:03:04.080 align:start position:19%
more bodies, Datlov himself, Zena
Kolmagorova, and Rustam Slobodin. Their

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:08.080 align:start position:19%
poses told a story. They were crawling
back toward the tent when they collapsed

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:14.000 align:start position:19%
and died. Slabodin's skull was
fractured, yet his skin was unbroken, as

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:18.480 align:start position:19%
if struck by an immense invisible force.
Five bodies recovered, but four hikers

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:23.519 align:start position:19%
were still missing somewhere in the
frozen wilderness. It took two more

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:28.480 align:start position:19%
months. Only when the spring came did
the mountain surrender its darkest

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:36.400 align:start position:19%
secret. In a ravine under 4 meters of
snow lay the last four.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:41.200 align:start position:19%
Dubanina, Kovatov, Tibo Brignol,
and Zolitario. Their injuries were

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:45.360 align:start position:19%
horrific. Crushed ribs, fractured
skulls, yet with barely a scratch on

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:51.040 align:start position:19%
their skin. Then came the detail that
haunts every investigator. Ludmila

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:55.360 align:start position:19%
Dubilina's tongue was missing, torn out.
Two others were missing their eyes, and

00:03:53.280 --> 00:04:00.319 align:start position:19%
their skin had turned a strange,
unnatural orange brown color. Strangest

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:04.640 align:start position:19%
of all, their clothing was highly
radioactive, as if dusted with something

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:09.760 align:start position:19%
from a nuclear test. The official
inquest ended with a sentence that

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:14.159 align:start position:19%
solved nothing. A compelling natural
force killed them. The files were

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:18.079 align:start position:19%
sealed. The region was closed for 3
years, and the questions only

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:22.160 align:start position:19%
multiplied. So, what really happened on
the dead mountain that night? The

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:27.840 align:start position:19%
theories range from science to the
impossible. Theory one, an avalanche. In

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:32.080 align:start position:19%
2021, Swiss scientists showed a rare
slab avalanche could explain the tense

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:36.800 align:start position:19%
damage. A slab avalanche could crush
ribs and skulls without breaking skin,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:42.479 align:start position:19%
matching the injuries in the ravine.
Theory two, paradoxical undressing. In

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:48.479 align:start position:19%
late hypothermia, the freezing brain
feels burning heat. Victim's strip. That

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:54.000 align:start position:19%
explains the underwear, the bare feet,
but not the slash tent, the crushed

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:58.800 align:start position:19%
bones, or the radiation. Theory three,
infrasound. A rare wind vortex over the

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:04.320 align:start position:19%
peak can drive humans into blind,
irrational panic. Colatyakle's shape is

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:08.800 align:start position:19%
perfect for it, but infrasound doesn't
fracture skulls or dust clothed with

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:14.240 align:start position:19%
radiation. Then the darker theories
begin. The Many people called the

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:20.720 align:start position:19%
mountain forbidden, cursed ground, home
of spirits. Theory four, secret military

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:26.080 align:start position:19%
tests. The Urals hid Soviet weapon
sites, and the hiker's camera caught

00:05:23.039 --> 00:05:31.520 align:start position:19%
strange lights. Other hikers miles away
reported glowing fire orbs drifting over

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:37.039 align:start position:19%
the peaks that very night. Coincidence?
The radiation fuels this theory. Fallout

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:43.199 align:start position:19%
from a failed test, a weapon no one will
admit existed. and the orange skin. Some

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:48.880 align:start position:19%
say chemical burns. Some say the flash
of something exploding in the sky.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:54.400 align:start position:19%
Theory five. The man spoke of the mink,
a giant wild creature of the deep

00:05:51.199 --> 00:06:00.400 align:start position:19%
forest. A yeti-ike beast could slash a
tent, crush a skull, and vanish without

00:05:57.039 --> 00:06:07.440 align:start position:19%
a trace. Yet no tracks were ever found.
Dubanina lay face down in a stream for 2

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:12.800 align:start position:19%
months. Nature, not monsters, may
explain the crulest details. In 2019,

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:18.479 align:start position:19%
Russia reopened the case. Their
conclusion, an avalanche. Case closed.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:22.319 align:start position:19%
The families were furious. An avalanche
doesn't explain the radiation. It

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:27.840 align:start position:19%
doesn't explain the fire orbs. It
doesn't explain the fear. In 2020, the

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:32.720 align:start position:19%
pass was officially renamed Datlov Pass,
honoring the leader who never led his

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:37.520 align:start position:19%
team home. Every year, new expeditions
climb the dead mountain, chasing the

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:42.960 align:start position:19%
truth through the same deadly cold. They
find the same things. The slope, the

00:06:39.919 --> 00:06:48.160 align:start position:19%
wind, the silence, and a mystery that
refuses to die. We know the injuries

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:54.880 align:start position:19%
were violent, the radiation was real,
and the official story explains almost

00:06:50.800 --> 00:07:01.919 align:start position:19%
nothing. A slab of snow, a weapon test
gone wrong, a panic no science has

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:07.120 align:start position:19%
named, or something older. Udin, the one
who turned back, spent his life

00:07:03.919 --> 00:07:11.680 align:start position:19%
searching for answers. He died in 2013.
The Diatlov Pass incident remains the

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:17.199 align:start position:19%
gold standard of unsolved mysteries.
Every answer births two new questions.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:23.360 align:start position:19%
Perhaps the truth is a perfect storm.
Avalanche, wind, cold, and panic. Each

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:28.960 align:start position:19%
harmless alone, lethal together. Or
perhaps the dead mountain guards a

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:35.440 align:start position:19%
secret no expedition, no laboratory, no
government will ever reveal. Nine young

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:41.360 align:start position:19%
lives full of courage and laughter.
Ended in a riddle written in snow and

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:46.000 align:start position:19%
silence. The mountain is still there.
The wind is still there. And the

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:49.840 align:start position:19%
question is still there waiting. What do
you believe happened that night? Tell us

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:55.199 align:start position:19%
in the comments. The best theories get
featured. If this mystery gave you

00:07:51.919 --> 00:08:00.479 align:start position:19%
chills, subscribe to Unsolved Shadows, a
new unsolved case every single day.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:04.560 align:start position:19%
Tomorrow, five children vanish from
their beds on Christmas Eve and the

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:09.280 align:start position:19%
house that should have burned them. The
Solder children were never found. Their

00:08:07.039 --> 00:08:16.160 align:start position:19%
mother believed they were stolen, and
she may have been right. Nine hikers,

00:08:12.479 --> 00:08:21.599 align:start position:19%
one mountain, zero answers. This was the
Datlov Pass incident. I'm asking you one

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:26.879 align:start position:19%
last time. What scared them out of that
tent? The mountain knows. It isn't

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:31.199 align:start position:19%
telling. Thanks for watching. Sleep well
tonight if you can. We'll see you in the

00:08:28.879 --> 00:08:31.199 align:start position:19%
shadows

